Accessibility

1. **Automated scanning (fast, catches ~30% of issues)**

Run one of these on every page:

axe DevTools (browser extension) or WAVE (wave.webaim.org) — free, catches missing alt text, contrast failures, missing labels, ARIA misuse
Lighthouse (built into Chrome DevTools → Accessibility tab)

🔵 https://i.imgur.com/AoQImJU.png

🔵 https://i.imgur.com/G5a8bQD.png

Pa11y or axe-core if you want it in a CI pipeline

These won't catch everything — they can't judge whether alt text is meaningful, or whether tab order makes sense. That needs manual testing.

✅ Most of the page 95% have labels/text 
❌ Some of the checkbox, small button (witout text) Should have labels

2. **Keyboard-only navigation**

Unplug the mouse. Tab through the entire page:

Can you reach every interactive element (links, buttons, form fields, custom widgets)?
Is the focus order logical (matches visual/reading order)?
Is there always a visible focus indicator?
Can you operate everything with Enter/Space/Arrow keys — no mouse-only traps?
In modals/dropdowns: does focus move in, get trapped inside while open, and return to the trigger on close?


✅ I tested the supplier portal and found that almost all of it, about 99%, can be navigated using a keyboard. But need to check all pages


3. **Screen reader testing**

Use a real screen reader, not just automated tools:

VoiceOver (Mac/iOS, built-in, Cmd+F5)
NVDA (Windows, free)
TalkBack (Android)

Navigate by headings, landmarks, and form fields. Check that everything is announced with a sensible name, role, and state (e.g. "Submit, button" not just "button").

✅ Tested with Edge's tool (compliant with W3C) it is compatible



4. **Color contrast**
 Body text: 4.5:1 minimum against background
 Large text (18px+ bold or 24px+): 3:1
 UI components/icons/borders: 3:1
 Tools: WebAIM Contrast Checker, or the contrast checker built into Chrome DevTools/Figma plugins

Supplier Portal Dark Theme
---------------------------------------

**Header**
- **"Primark Stores Ltd"** (bold title, white on dark teal) — contrast ~14:1 ✅
- **"Packaging compliance portal"** (subtitle, muted gray-teal on dark teal) — contrast ~2.2:1 ❌ (fails AA, needs 4.5:1)
- **"Products" nav pill** (active, bright green text on dark teal pill) — contrast ~7.8:1 ✅
- **"Packaging Components" / "Supporting Documents"** (inactive nav text, light gray on dark teal) — contrast ~8.9:1 ✅
- **"Due:" label** (muted gray-blue on dark teal) — contrast ~2.1:1 ❌ (fails AA)
- **"26 Jul 2026"** (orange date value on dark teal) — contrast ~7.1:1 ✅


